# OneSignal (TRYST)

## Layout

```
lib/onesignal/
  config.ts      # NEXT_PUBLIC_ONESIGNAL_APP_ID + REST key
  types.ts       # Notify kinds / payloads
  activeChat.ts  # Suppress when match chat is open
  client.ts      # Browser helpers → /api/onesignal/*
  server.ts      # REST create notification (server only)
app/api/onesignal/
  notify/route.ts    # Send push to external_id
  register/route.ts  # Save player/subscription ids
components/tryst/
  OneSignalProvider.tsx      # Init + permission + suppress
  IncomingCallListener.tsx   # Global call invite UI
public/OneSignalSDKWorker.js
supabase/onesignal_player_id.sql
```

## Rules

- App ID is public (`NEXT_PUBLIC_ONESIGNAL_APP_ID`). REST API key is **server-only** (`ONESIGNAL_REST_API_KEY`).
- Never commit real REST keys. Put them only in `.env.local`.
- External ID = TRYST `users.id` via `OneSignal.login(userId)`.
- **Suppress**: if `getActiveChatMatchId() === matchId`, do not show push (`foregroundWillDisplay` + skip in-app toast for that chat).
- Message / audio / video call pushes go through `POST /api/onesignal/notify` after send/startCall.
- Run `supabase/onesignal_player_id.sql` once so `onesignal_player_id` columns exist.

## Notify kinds

`message` | `audio_call` | `video_call` | `match` | `like` | `generic`

## Permission

Ask once after auth via `OneSignal.Slidedown.promptPush()` (fallback `requestPermission`).
